Description: Tolerate MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC being set in TestSCMCredentials
 On some build-sandbox kernels ReadMsgUnix's returned flags carry
 MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC (0x40000000) even though the test only sent SCM_CREDENTIALS
 ancillary data (no file descriptors, so nothing for O_CLOEXEC to apply to).
 That flag is set by the net package's own socket handling, not by anything
 this package (golang.org/x/sys/unix) implements or that this test exercises,
 and the test's actual subject -- the SCM_CREDENTIALS bytes round-tripping
 correctly -- still passes. Same rationale and same upstream-test-fragility
 pattern as 03-skip-TestOpenByHandleAt-if-openMountByID-fails.patch already
 in this series: fail the build on a real defect in this package's own code,
 not on a build-sandbox-dependent kernel/runtime detail this package does not
 control.
Author: DANOS <noreply@danos.io>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-28
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/unix/creds_test.go
+++ b/unix/creds_test.go
@@ -92,8 +92,10 @@
 		if err != nil {
 			t.Fatalf("ReadMsgUnix: %v", err)
 		}
-		if flags != 0 {
-			t.Fatalf("ReadMsgUnix flags = 0x%x, want 0", flags)
+		if flags&^unix.MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC != 0 {
+			t.Fatalf("ReadMsgUnix flags = 0x%x, want 0 (or only MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC)", flags)
+		} else if flags != 0 {
+			t.Logf("ReadMsgUnix flags = 0x%x (MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC set by this kernel/sandbox; no fds were sent, so ignoring)", flags)
 		}
 		if n != tt.dataLen {
 			t.Fatalf("ReadMsgUnix n = %d, want %d", n, tt.dataLen)
